From: Yar1klamer
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add Samsung S5K4H7 sensor driver

The S5K4H7 is an 8 MP (3264x2448, 1.12 um) RAW10 Bayer sensor with a
4-lane MIPI CSI-2 interface, used as the front camera of the Lenovo Tab
P11 (TB-J606F). There is no public datasheet; the register settings
come from the stock CamX sensor module of the tablet, which carries a
single 3264x2448 mode at 30 fps: 24 MHz MCLK, 272 MHz pixel rate,
732 Mbps per lane (366 MHz link frequency).

The driver follows the s5k3m5 driver: CCI register access, runtime PM,
exposure, analogue gain (0x20 = 1x up to 16x), vertical blanking,
horizontal and vertical flip (which change the Bayer order), the
sensor test patterns and the crop selection targets.

Tested on the TB-J606F: the colour bar pattern decodes as GRBG with a
black level of 64, and libcamera's simple pipeline streams 3264x2448 at
30.03 fps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
